ctive videos and real-world scenarios help clarify complex topics such as agile-compatible contracts and cross-functional team dynamics. Special sections on mock exams and certification tips provide a focused pathway to acing the PSPO II® exam. Whether you're fine-tuning your understanding of Scrum artifacts or learning to navigate challenging stakeholder scenarios, this course provides the expertise and confidence to succeed as a Product Owner. By the end of this course, you'll not only be prepared to pass the PSPO II® exam but also to drive innovation and value within your Agile teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agilescrummasterlevelii_certificationprepwithmockexams"&gt;&lt;a id="agilescrummasterlevelii_certificationprepwithmockexams" href="https://youtu.be/FVIW8hnX11M"&gt;Agile Scrum Master Level II - Certification Prep with Mock Exams: Master Agile Leadership with Advanced Scrum Practices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Advance your Scrum knowledge and skills with this Level II course tailored for aspiring leaders in Agile environments. Covering advanced topics such as empiricism, team dynamics, stakeholder engagement, and risk management, this course also includes mock exams to ensure you're exam-ready. Become a certified expert in Scrum and lead with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Dive into the core principles of Scrum, exploring empiricism, Scrum values, and the intricacies of self-management. You’ll learn how to navigate the dynamics of Scrum teams, handle challenging stakeholder interactions, and foster collaboration across scaled teams. Each module features practical scenarios, quizzes, and actionable strategies to solidify your understanding. The course doesn’t just focus on theory—it’s a hands-on learning experience. Delve into the nuances of Scrum events, artifacts, and the all-important Definition of Done, ensuring you have a holistic grasp of every Scrum facet. Discover how to mitigate risks, tackle technical debt, and build resilient teams. Practical tips for exam preparation and mock tests are woven throughout to help you succeed on your first attempt at the PSM II® certification. By the end of this course, you’ll be equipped with the skills to lead Agile transformations confidently. With insights into leadership, organizational culture, and facilitation, this course ensures you’re not just exam-ready but also prepared to elevate your professional impact as a Scrum Master.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrumrepairguide_getagileteamsbackontrack"&gt;&lt;a id="scrumrepairguide_getagileteamsbackontrack" href="https://youtu.be/H-vyQCv253E"&gt;The Scrum Repair Guide - Get Agile Teams Back on Track: Restore Agile Team Performance with Practical Scrum Repair Techniques&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many Scrum teams stall due to rigid practices, vague goals, or poor collaboration. This course helps you assess your team's health, uncover root causes, and implement proven solutions. Reignite performance by realigning with true Scrum values and practical techniques.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Agile success isn’t about rigidly following best practices—it’s about evolving your Scrum team in a way that fits your organization’s goals, structure, and people. This course begins by guiding you through a self-assessment to uncover why your team may be struggling, from misaligned goals to over-management and low morale. It identifies the common traps that teams fall into and explains how to correct them without abandoning the core framework of Scrum. You’ll move through real-world problem-solving sessions, combining strategic insights with hands-on exercises. You'll revisit Scrum’s foundational values and learn how to operationalize them in retrospectives and decision-making. You’ll fix your Product Backlog, restructure roles like the Product Owner, and uncover the real cause behind team stagnation. Developers, managers, and product leads will benefit from actionable strategies to rebuild accountability, collaboration, and clarity across the entire Scrum cycle. By the end of the course, you won’t just have a better understanding of Scrum—you’ll have a customized toolkit to repair dysfunctions, align stakeholders, and empower your team to deliver high-value results sprint after sprint. Whether you’re rebooting a struggling team or proactively optimizing performance, this guide is your blueprint to long-term agility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="masteringagilescrum_frombasicstoadvancedwithjiraprojects"&gt;&lt;a id="masteringagilescrum_frombasicstoadvancedwithjiraprojects" href="https://youtu.be/3oDb79JGg8c"&gt;Mastering Agile Scrum - From Basics to Advanced with Jira Projects: Master Agile, Scrum, and Jira for Modern Project Management Success&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gain a complete understanding of Agile Scrum and how to apply it effectively in real-world projects. This course explores Scrum roles, events, artifacts, and workflows, enhanced with Jira-based implementation. Learn to plan, execute, and refine agile projects with confidence and precision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In today’s fast-paced digital world, mastering Agile and Scrum is vital for effective project management. This course introduces the Scrum framework, its core values, and principles, exploring how Agile overcomes common challenges like poor coordination and inefficient planning. You’ll learn about the roles of the Scrum Master, Product Owner, and Development Team, and gain hands-on experience with creating user stories, estimating workloads, and defining the “Definition of Done.” The course covers managing product and sprint backlogs, conducting sprints, and using tools like burndown charts to track progress. You’ll also gain experience with Jira, setting up boards, epics, and tracking sprint performance. By the end, you’ll understand how to scale Scrum across multiple teams, facilitate Scrum ceremonies, and compare frameworks like SAFe and DAD. This course will help you lead Agile transformations, refine backlogs iteratively, and improve delivery and innovation for better project outcomes. Perfect for team leaders, developers, and project managers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="ai-enhancedscrummaster_automateanalyseandaccelerateagileworkflow"&gt;&lt;a id="ai-enhancedscrummaster_automateanalyseandaccelerateagileworkflow" href="https://youtu.be/HuJ-da2F8gQ"&gt;The AI-Enhanced Scrum Master - Automate, Analyse, and Accelerate Agile Workflow: Unlock Agile Excellence with Generative AI: Streamline, Automate, and Scale Scrum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The AI-Enhanced Scrum Master course teaches you to leverage Generative AI tools to streamline Agile processes. From backlog creation to sprint planning and ceremonies, you'll learn to automate tasks, boost team productivity, and integrate AI with tools like Jira, ChatGPT, and Microsoft Copilot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course is designed for Scrum Masters and Agile practitioners eager to embrace the power of Generative AI to supercharge their workflows. This course covers everything from automating backlog creation, user story generation, and sprint planning to enhancing Scrum ceremonies like daily standups. You’ll start by learning the fundamentals of Generative AI, including tools like ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini, and how to apply them in an Agile context. With practical examples, you’ll explore prompt engineering, AI-driven prioritization, and how to integrate AI tools within Jira and other popular platforms. Key highlights include automating user story creation, generating acceptance criteria, and using AI for sprint tracking with burndown charts and dashboards. You’ll also learn ethical considerations around AI adoption and how to drive AI acceptance within your teams. By the end of the course, you'll be equipped to leverage AI for improved decision-making, team collaboration, and overall Agile success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrummastercrashcourse_advancedpreparationforthepsmiicertification"&gt;&lt;a id="scrummastercrashcourse_advancedpreparationforthepsmiicertification" href="https://youtu.be/7hsfHRIl2-c"&gt;Scrum Master Crash Course - Advanced Preparation for the PSM II Certification: Advance Your Scrum Mastery, Leadership Skills, and Agile Thinking for PSM-A Certification&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/39c1e734d5672c436f4e8f5df73199d800141f70.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=012f519c34bfea317b97b3c46d2307c1"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course strengthens advanced Scrum Master skills required for the PSM-A certification. It focuses on leadership, product management, and professional Scrum practices beyond the basics. Designed to help experienced practitioners apply Scrum effectively in complex environments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Disclaimer: Scrum Open, Professional Scrum, Professional Scrum Master, Professional Scrum Product Owner, PSM, PSM I, PSM II, PSM 1, PSM 2, PSPO, and related terms are registered trademarks of Advanced Development Methods, Inc., doing business as Scrum.org. Our course and practice exams are neither endorsed by nor affiliated with Scrum.org. This course builds on core Scrum foundations and revisits Agile values, Scrum theory, roles, events, and artifacts, then expands into people development, servant leadership, and real-world Scrum Master challenges. Emphasis is placed on decision-making, accountability, and applying empiricism beyond theory. As the journey progresses, the focus shifts to managing products with agility and supporting value delivery at scale. Topics such as product vision, backlog management, forecasting, release planning, and continuous quality provide a strong understanding of how Scrum Masters collaborate with Product Owners and Development Teams. The final stages emphasize mastery through advanced tips, coaching techniques, and organizational agility. Learners explore how to influence culture, enable evidence-based management, and foster sustainable, high-performing teams. Ideal for experienced Scrum Masters preparing for PSM-A, with basic Scrum knowledge and hands-on experience strongly recommended.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="aiprojectmanagementskills_scrummasterplusaipluschatgptplusjira_enh"&gt;&lt;a id="aiprojectmanagementskills_scrummasterplusaipluschatgptplusjira_enh" href="https://youtu.be/mKM9aK4WL-o"&gt;AI Project Management skills - Scrum Master+AI+ChatGPT+Jira: Enhance Scrum Master Practices with AI, ChatGPT, and Jira&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/236f74a3eb80b9094a6391e2f2d51249cdd00fca.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2252d0384227e1f851e1ac0ad3c5e597"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course teaches Scrum Masters how to integrate AI into Agile project management. Learn to use ChatGPT, Jira AI, and modern tools to support product goals, backlog creation, sprint planning, and team facilitation. Gain practical, ethical, and repeatable AI-driven workflows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course focuses on applying AI to real Scrum Master responsibilities using ChatGPT, Jira, and complementary AI tools. You’ll begin by understanding the role of AI in Agile environments, including prompt engineering fundamentals and how to select the right AI tools for project management tasks. Next, you’ll learn how to facilitate product goal creation and refinement using ChatGPT. The course then moves into AI-assisted product backlog management, where you’ll generate backlogs, acceptance criteria, and estimates, and seamlessly integrate them into Jira. You’ll also explore how Jira AI and ChatGPT can support sprint planning, subtask creation, capacity planning, and team commitment. In the final sections, you’ll apply AI throughout the sprint lifecycle. You’ll learn how to combine human judgment with AI outputs, generate meeting transcriptions, track actions in Jira and Confluence, and identify recurring blockers using ChatGPT. By the end of the course, you’ll be equipped to responsibly use AI to enhance Scrum facilitation, improve efficiency, and support better team outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="certifiedagilepractitionerpmi-acprtraining_prepareforthepmi-acprex"&gt;&lt;a id="certifiedagilepractitionerpmi-acprtraining_prepareforthepmi-acprex" href="https://youtu.be/cBXm68egvjE"&gt;Certified Agile Practitioner (PMI-ACP(r)) Training: Prepare for the PMI-ACP(r) Exam with Comprehensive Agile Training and Real-World Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/a212ff2ab55fd83322c9983b13612dc6e396a212.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=1f0756247f70ec700deaba4d582c2bff"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This comprehensive course will guide you through the Agile principles and practices required to become a Certified Agile Practitioner (PMI-ACP®). Gain real-world experience with Agile frameworks like Scrum, Kanban, and Lean while preparing for the PMI-ACP® exam. Hands-on exercises and project examples help reinforce learning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; The Certified Agile Practitioner (PMI-ACP®) Training course is designed to prepare you for the PMI-ACP® certification exam and help you gain a deep understanding of Agile methodologies. Starting with an introduction to Agile principles, the course dives into core practices like Scrum, Lean, Kanban, and eXtreme Programming (XP), and covers essential topics like Agile mindset, leadership, and team collaboration. Through detailed modules, you'll explore key topics such as the 12 Agile principles, project planning and execution, risk management, and product delivery. The course also offers practical insights into Agile frameworks, leadership styles, and how to foster a collaborative team environment. You’ll walk through real-world examples and projects, matched with the ACP exam content outline, to ensure your readiness. The course culminates in preparing you for the PMI-ACP® exam, providing essential guidance on exam application and how to navigate audit situations. By the end, you’ll not only be well-prepared for the certification but also equipped to apply Agile methodologies in real-world projects and work environments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agilescrummastercertificationbootcamp_psmiandcsm_transformyourcare"&gt;&lt;a id="agilescrummastercertificationbootcamp_psmiandcsm_transformyourcare" href="https://youtu.be/0fABxCVUB3c"&gt;Agile Scrum Master Certification Bootcamp - PSM I and CSM: Transform Your Career with Scrum Master Certification - PSM I &amp; CSM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6520aa26365f270a1ae92c763b8a26a37e179000.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=0396eb32128ce22fa8df44058a5179a6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Become an expert in Agile Scrum with this comprehensive certification bootcamp. Prepare for PSM I and CSM exams while mastering Scrum practices and frameworks. Build the skills to lead successful teams in Agile environments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This bootcamp provides an in-depth exploration of Agile Scrum and prepares you for the PSM I and CSM certifications. The course covers everything from Agile fundamentals to Scrum frameworks, teaching you how to effectively manage projects and teams in a dynamic environment. Through detailed modules, you'll explore Scrum's values, principles, and the various roles within a Scrum team, providing you with a well-rounded understanding of how Scrum operates in practice. The course then takes you through Scrum events, artifacts, and commitments, ensuring you’re equipped with the knowledge to plan, execute, and review Scrum processes successfully. Real-world examples and practical exercises help reinforce the learning, ensuring you understand how to apply Scrum in diverse scenarios. With expert guidance, you'll master techniques for managing backlogs, coaching teams, and resolving challenges, all while preparing for the certification exams. The final part of the course focuses on helping you pass the PSM I and CSM exams, providing tips, sample questions, and exam strategies. With step-by-step guidance, you'll be ready to confidently pursue certification and embark on a successful Scrum Master career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="aiproductmanagerskillsforagile_aiproductmanagement_masteraiproduct"&gt;&lt;a id="aiproductmanagerskillsforagile_aiproductmanagement_masteraiproduct" href="https://youtu.be/E6ISdwN8UFo"&gt;AI Product Manager Skills for Agile - AI Product Management: Master AI Product Management in an Agile Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/f654a93c3e5aa255cde6f546c827f41e5e992c26.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5ea56572c0f98edfd0d09c774450b579"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course teaches AI product management skills for Agile teams, covering prompt engineering, competitive analysis, backlog management with Jira, and sprint planning. Learn how to create product roadmaps, define product strategy, and manage AI product lifecycles effectively in an Agile environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In this course, learners will dive into the core skills necessary for AI product management within Agile methodologies. Starting with the fundamentals, you will explore the birth of AI, understand why product managers need prompt engineering, and get hands-on with tools like ChatGPT. The first section offers a foundational understanding of AI tools and their uses in product management. The next section focuses on market research techniques vital for successful product management, including capturing user data and conducting competitive analysis. You will gain essential insights into analyzing user comments and reviews, preparing deep competitive analysis, and understanding market dynamics, which are crucial for making informed decisions in AI product management. As you advance, you'll learn to create a compelling AI product vision, strategy, and roadmap. Discover how to align product development with Agile principles and create a structured product backlog. Through hands-on exercises in Jira, you’ll gain practical experience in managing AI product backlogs, setting sprint goals, and using transcriptions to enhance collaboration. By the end of this course, you’ll be well-equipped to handle AI product lifecycle management effectively.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrumandleaninaction_modernagileprojectleadership_masteragileandle"&gt;&lt;a id="scrumandleaninaction_modernagileprojectleadership_masteragileandle" href="https://youtu.be/K4teitv7UrI"&gt;Scrum &amp; Lean in Action - Modern Agile Project Leadership: Master Agile and Lean Methodologies for Effective Project Management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/39c4e6e9f28360a66d40625e9f864b5cb8d6ad37.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=b66d898ae508e5eb5e33c7a4809ce086"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course covers Agile and Lean principles, focusing on project leadership in real-world scenarios. You'll learn how to manage Agile projects, understand customer personas, and apply Lean strategies for process improvement. Gain essential skills in project estimation, prioritization, and Agile ceremonies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In this course, you’ll start with a strong foundation of Agile and Lean principles, examining the core differences between Agile and Waterfall methodologies. The course delves into customer-centric project management, introducing you to customer personas, user stories, and acceptance criteria to ensure you're meeting client needs from day one. You will also explore MoSCoW prioritization and minimum viable product (MVP) strategies to ensure your projects stay on track and deliver value. As you progress, you’ll dive into managing Agile projects with a focus on roles, reviews, metrics, and risk management. Learn the best practices for building Agile work breakdown structures (WBS) and identifying the right tasks and milestones for your team. The course also provides a deep understanding of Lean concepts like work-in-progress (WIP) limits, Kaizen, and Little’s Law, essential for streamlining workflows and improving productivity. By the end of the course, you'll be equipped with actionable insights on both Agile and Lean practices that will help you lead projects successfully. Whether you’re managing a team or collaborating with stakeholders, this course will transform your approach to modern project leadership, making you a proficient leader who can effectively handle Agile projects and processes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
