      <description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/644b2860fe24424a4e6a9b1f016bfb9825b7c116.png?auto=compress,format&amp;h=340&amp;w=1200&amp;s=a3cb3ab9509255907214eb38ba4d4b98"&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/172f8ef24d630275f6062e3a401c8713ff0858a6.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=crop&amp;h=600&amp;w=1200&amp;s=bdf6151b19d7b73eb1b14b89071e5be6"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Build a portfolio in a weekend!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Calling all game developers—build a portfolio of intriguing game sets, environments, and situations lightning‑fast with the Portfolio in a Weekend Bundle by CG Cookie! Pay what you want for detailed set textures like flowing curtains and beams of light, realistic museum environments, and even believable dice‑rolling animations. Unlock a diverse library of game development assets designed for speed‑to‑market game development from the pros at CG Cookie, and help support Save the Children when you shop with Humble Bundle!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#0"&gt;Pay $25 to unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#planet"&gt;Planet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#loopingpatterns"&gt;Looping Patterns&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#graphiclandscape"&gt;Graphic Landscape&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#lightshapehallway"&gt;Light Shape Hallway&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#museum"&gt;Museum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#ancientpillars"&gt;Ancient Pillars&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#diceroll"&gt;Dice Roll&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#oceaninslowmotion"&gt;Ocean in Slow Motion&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#dewdroplet"&gt;Dew Droplet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#yin-yangpencils"&gt;Yin-Yang Pencils&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#piano"&gt;Piano&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#laptop"&gt;Laptop&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#blurredlines"&gt;Blurred Lines&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#glasstiles"&gt;Glass Tiles&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#moltenreveal"&gt;Molten Reveal&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#fillswitch"&gt;Fill Switch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#keycaps"&gt;Key Caps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#simplestep"&gt;Simple Step&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#morningcoffee"&gt;Morning Coffee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#flowingcurtain"&gt;Flowing Curtain&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#marblecolonade"&gt;Marble Colonade&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#cabinwithaview"&gt;Cabin with a View&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#forgottenroom"&gt;Forgotten Room&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 id="0"&gt;Pay $25 to unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="planet"&gt;&lt;a id="planet" href="https://youtu.be/VMcPQAugkEc"&gt;Planet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/85fbf2e4974c4ad3c8987aa1bb37e38d280e1e07.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5f2b97c2e1ad8d1e05a676ce00f71020"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Monochromatic outer space. Can you feel the drama? This scene is designed to inspire cinematic awe. Discover how the most basic, primitive geometry can look incredible with the right materials and lighting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="loopingpatterns"&gt;&lt;a id="loopingpatterns"&gt;Looping Patterns&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6347d93c10b286623d4c8f0851112b869912a8de.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=ef6b9d344e3c1a982308ecb8860211c1"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Utilizing procedural textures to generate animated loops for practical and artistic purposes. This chapter features four distinct looping patterns, each building on the principles of the previous.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="graphiclandscape"&gt;&lt;a id="graphiclandscape"&gt;Graphic Landscape&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/7d9e519f69f8093afac95aedefd840a2dca81a3a.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=a4968cf23eb4c241fb35428b5b532f81"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create an adorable graphic environment that loops endlessly between day and night. Zero light objects are used, meaning every shade of color is achieved with shader nodes. Render times are zippity zoppity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="lightshapehallway"&gt;&lt;a id="lightshapehallway"&gt;Light Shape Hallway&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/bb56fee74c3e1ac0a53091a34dbdce333cca4be1.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=7098ba1e4958234249ab791220180465"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Semi-abstract exercise that explores the visual interest of shapes cast by light and shadow. The setup is fast, simple, freeform, and wide-open to iteration.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="museum"&gt;&lt;a id="museum"&gt;Museum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/ed391793f58a5e5343b08e9554d1e5e629b6556c.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=4a351337a892fc2411b69c3e13517a2f"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A more grounded application of the light shape hallway exercise that leans into photorealistic interior spaces. Another example of basic shapes looking better than they should with competent materials and interesting lighting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="ancientpillars"&gt;&lt;a id="ancientpillars"&gt;Ancient Pillars&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/b02e833088ae64a0cef050698d48a6d1aec6cd04.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=d02ec96bf298925c8739e2dae0b0b7d4"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Can we create a realistic environment that feels enormous using minimalistic techniques?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yes. Yes we can.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="diceroll"&gt;&lt;a id="diceroll" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Dice Roll&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/e13d6368f99f206d417000e42509f172e09360cd.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=69a986bfbf3afa4d3f0f04d789b58e6e"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;A symbol of trying your luck; taking a risk. This project is a fun introduction to the macro aesthetic, where high fidelity detail is paramount and bokeh blur narrows viewer focus. Rigid body simulation also makes a cameo.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="oceaninslowmotion"&gt;&lt;a id="oceaninslowmotion" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Ocean in Slow Motion&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/e8dcd75c5a62a76ab4c6aea92aa06e891a199ef9.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=92ba0768e0a05acb565ceeacb449ba7b"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manifest the slow down, bright sunny vibes of summer. Learn to utilize Blender's ocean modifier to simulate body-of-water behavior. Then discover the trick to make that behavior loop seamlessly. And finally, capture mesmerizing bokeh shapes as they dance on the water's surface.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="dewdroplet"&gt;&lt;a id="dewdroplet" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Dew Droplet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/92e5ae47e15c7702ec4da0faf89d4f4ae43dba98.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=b0b49e6966e55f8a4638c38698335144"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Craft the peace and tranquility of early morning. This project draws your attention to the beautiful details of leafy organics. We will utilize micropolygon displacement for maximum geometric fidelity. Along with simple rigging and f-curve modifier power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="yin-yangpencils"&gt;&lt;a id="yin-yangpencils" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Yin-Yang Pencils&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/b6166f72a26e5381c133f946686e41462914fb58.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=e8ec265d8da6425b539f3fac88dc3a31"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Embrace complimentary contrast in this simple, satisfying animation. Unlike other macro projects, depth of field is not applicable here. Instead we will lean on micropolygon displacement to achieve a believable level of detail at such a close proximity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="piano"&gt;&lt;a id="piano" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Piano&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/0af934a7de26b619f7ff2197c72aaaf3f307b0c8.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=26afe95f31c891793463e4f943ca801e"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;An elegant, timeless instrument with repetitive shape complexity - perfect for fast creation. The material plays a key role in tactile realism while the glowing orbs serve as unique flare and interesting bokeh fodder.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="laptop"&gt;&lt;a id="laptop" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Laptop&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/844ed80016b202153005c11e4e1cb83aada31bd5.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=1217681c3af342a26df8e934d93ea72f"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Blurring the lines between the macro and product rendering genres. Or should I say bokeh blurring the lines...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="blurredlines"&gt;&lt;a id="blurredlines" href="https://youtu.be/uEPFOUA15tw"&gt;Blurred Lines&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/3a9c4f1d7597ae3cd0397a26977d2642ddb0d4c7.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=b8a081451c8db58adf377d38d4fbc0bb"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Kick off the course with a simple project that artistically obscures rotating text behind an array of glass cylinders. It's the first example of easy concepts that radically affect the final result.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="glasstiles"&gt;&lt;a id="glasstiles"&gt;Glass Tiles&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/5e812a0cbeb0d126f1d5b0d551be5d7b9b4c7fa5.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=4b9a88805d7a4c2da4738aa1905822fd"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This project is a spiritual successor to the first, demonstrating how relatively small tweaks to a creative concept can result in very different aesthetics. This time Kaizen eases into Geometry Nodes to generate a glass tile grid.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="moltenreveal"&gt;&lt;a id="moltenreveal" href="https://youtu.be/sJfSmtM8oQI"&gt;Molten Reveal&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/c84648cd48ed73b15a5e4b410a3c44c7e18578b5.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=17eaa45f18ec84ea28264f14082ae3d4"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;We've tasted the power of Geometry Nodes but now it's time for a complete meal! This cinematic title reveal transitions from molten lava to cooled metal. The perfect style for that movie you're working on&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="fillswitch"&gt;&lt;a id="fillswitch"&gt;Fill Switch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/16aafff5fed6e4384debf257d56adaa71fd591a4.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2fb9cee12e3eeef4a427b382f07a5b00"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Another project based in Geometry Nodes. The animation utilizes proximity to control the shape and movement of instances arranged in a typeface-specific string. The final result dynamic and emphasized.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="keycaps"&gt;&lt;a id="keycaps"&gt;Key Caps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/995de13fa778438a790a8ef0ca5cb3a1507b618b.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=8e48d74cb6e8196cb9837f8482b0e7ac"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The final and most abstract project. Learn to manipulate a grid of instanced keycaps while also applying a unique letter/character to each instance. You'll also see how to instance a certain word across the keys. Plus you can leverage the shader to transition from wireframe to realistic material.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="simplestep"&gt;&lt;a id="simplestep" href="https://youtu.be/VbHkJnVrz7I"&gt;Simple Step&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/5f0777f5b9e6befea24e3f828f7256f2b57775f0.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=ca23eb577f17ef04a51aff6e110ae995"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take the first step. The introduction into the interior vignettes focuses on just the architecture, with simple modeling techniques combined with modifiers. Learn how procedural textures combined with interesting lighting and reflections can make the most basic scene look compelling.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="morningcoffee"&gt;&lt;a id="morningcoffee"&gt;Morning Coffee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/41b4d68add524c832f56e1416fa69aa2fb43d1c5.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=a7f6d9a6db25d340984e16510eab8f9c"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Settle in with a warm brew. Increasing the complexity, this next scene grows richer and more tactile as we shape a soft, inviting rug with the geo-nodes hair system, let subtle procedural steam rise from our cup, and place simple exterior elements to paint the interior with expressive shadow patterns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="flowingcurtain"&gt;&lt;a id="flowingcurtain"&gt;Flowing Curtain&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/7381b7ef9a9fdf173d14fc19fedfa2d46d0ce8fa.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=37bc67b04b690b88e9cefd53ffe25cb6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turn your attention to a single, graceful subject: a curtain caught in the wind. Cloth simulation and wind forces shape its movement, procedural materials bring depth and texture, and a simple trick turns the motion into a seamless looping animation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="marblecolonade"&gt;&lt;a id="marblecolonade"&gt;Marble Colonade&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/beec7219c94b6d0aa1d8bd6a80d935e1abd19fb4.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=35527c103101df051aa0b8719da457db"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Travel back in time and visit an ancient temple. Subdivision surface techniques create elegant columns, while the true centerpiece is a procedural marble material which flows across every part of the scene. As the camera moves, shifting lights guide the eye, drawing attention exactly where the story wants it to rest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="cabinwithaview"&gt;&lt;a id="cabinwithaview"&gt;Cabin with a View&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/44988569c0c1bb5e31f4b76b68b16589266d0e1a.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=c44576a0e8aeb67f5b0e24c9dcdb2579"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Zooming out farther to reveal more of the room, this scene opens the interior toward the world beyond, where a simple image blends with the sky texture to suggest an inviting exterior. Bean bag chairs created using cloth simulation offer a relaxed place to settle in and watch the sunset unfold in a gentle time lapse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="forgottenroom"&gt;&lt;a id="forgottenroom"&gt;Forgotten Room&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/c457f2ab30217b189befc73357a44dc369bce7f7.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=c88e41e2b0cad68a8ecddbe0f8320572"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Uncover the mystery of the flowers in the forgotten house. Adapting pre-existing assets to fit the narrative, this project shifts the focus more towards the story-telling, utilizing particles dancing in atmospheric lighting and the power of the compositor to add the right amount of tension to the scene.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
